The Rust dependency sources are vendored under vendor so package builds
do not access the network. The vendor tree contains the locked dependencies
needed for the Linux amd64, arm64, and i386 targets.

The vendor tree includes Cargo.toml.orig files referenced by Cargo's checksum
metadata. debian/rules excludes vendor from dh_clean so these source files are
preserved across package builds.

The AWS-LC jitterentropy source must be compiled without optimization.
debian/rules preserves the Debian C compiler flags and appends -O0 for
AWS-LC's native build.

The vendored crates retain their upstream Cargo.toml files and license texts.
Before upload to a Debian or Ubuntu archive, review the dependency licensing
and replace vendored copies with archive-provided librust-* packages where
compatible. Crates or versions not yet in the archive may need to be packaged
separately.
